"about.brand" = "PlugLit";
"privacy.document" = "PlugLit Privacy Policy · Updated October 30, 2026\n\nOperator and contact\nDeveloped and operated by Wu Kai (吴凯). Privacy and support: feedback.pluglit@macseek.cc. Website: https://auv.macseek.cc.\n\nInformation used on your device\nPlugLit reads charging status and battery level to decide whether to start Keep Awake, update the display and stop playback when unplugged. This processing happens locally.\n\nLocal storage\nThe app remembers whether you have seen the guide and stores up to 200 events from the last 7 days (time, battery, charging and playback state). Expired events are excluded on reading or writing; old records are cleaned when the app opens. You can preview, export or clear them in Feedback. The diagnostics folder is excluded from system backups; uninstalling deletes local records. The app also writes system logs managed by your iOS settings.\n\nOptional feedback and diagnostics\nOnly after you enter feedback, consent and tap Send feedback are your description and optional email sent to https://auv.macseek.cc. Diagnostic attachments are off by default. If enabled, they also send the previewable model identifier (such as iPhone18,3), system/app versions, low-power and thermal state, battery and events. We do not read device names, serial numbers, UDIDs, advertising identifiers or other apps’ content. Feedback works without logs; not uploading does not affect Keep Awake.\n\nWebsite, storage and deletion\nThe website uses Cloudflare networking and storage; servers may be outside your country. HTTPS protects transmission. The network provider processes connection IP addresses; the feedback database does not store raw IP addresses. Feedback is used only for troubleshooting and replies. Online records are kept for 30 days and deleted by the next hourly cleanup after expiry; hosting providers may retain limited disaster-recovery data. Save your feedback reference to request immediate deletion of the online record on the feedback page. Do not share it publicly. Cloudflare privacy information: https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/. Do not include passwords, payment details or unrelated personal information.\n\nCollection and permissions\nThere are no accounts, ads or third-party analytics SDKs. The app does not access contacts, photos, microphone or location. The charging animation is bundled and plays offline. Descriptions, optional email and diagnostics are collected only when you submit them, never for advertising, tracking or data trading.\n\nShortcuts and external websites\nYou create and manage personal automations in Shortcuts. PlugLit cannot read or delete these rules. Website, other-app and version links open external services governed by their own privacy policies.\n\nDeletion and changes\nUninstalling removes local app data but not submitted feedback; use its reference on the website to delete it. iOS separately manages system logs, backups and personal automations. Disable or remove linked automations before uninstalling. Submit privacy questions and rights requests through the website’s feedback page. This policy will be updated if data processing changes.";
"terms.document" = "Please read before using PlugLit.\n\nScope\nPlugLit plays a charging animation with system Picture in Picture and keeps the display awake where supported. It does not change Auto-Lock duration or bypass passcodes or unlock restrictions. After playback stops, the system applies your existing lock settings.\n\nSystem limitations\nBehavior depends on iOS version, power, other media and system resources. Plugging in while locked may require unlocking first. Hiding, pausing or closing PiP may end Keep Awake. Continuous display is not guaranteed on every device or in every situation.\n\nResponsible use\nKeeping the display on and playing video increases power use and heat. Limit usage according to device temperature and surroundings. Stop when no longer needed. Do not rely on this app for critical tasks requiring an uninterrupted display.\n\nAutomations and disabling\nAutomatic operation on power changes requires rules you create in Shortcuts. Stopping playback does not disable future automations. Stop playback and remove the associated rules before uninstalling.\n\nUpdates and external services\nPublic iOS releases update through Apple’s App Store; test releases use TestFlight. The website accurately states when a release is not yet available. The app does not download or install executable code and does not use Sparkle. External sites and apps are operated by their respective providers. These terms do not limit your rights under applicable law.";
